---
alwaysApply: true
---
description: Angular and TypeScript coding standards
globs:

"src/**/*.ts"
"src/**/*.html"
alwaysApply: false
Angular
General
Use modern Angular APIs.
Use standalone components.
Use strict TypeScript.
Prefer signals for local reactive state when appropriate.
Use Angular dependency injection rather than manual service instantiation.
Use Angular Router for navigation.
Use lazy loading for appropriate feature routes.
Components
Keep components focused.
Avoid large monolithic components.
Avoid unnecessary abstraction.
Do not create a component unless it provides a clear benefit.
Prefer composition over inheritance.
Keep business logic out of templates.
TypeScript
Never use any unless there is a documented technical reason.
Prefer explicit interfaces and types.
Avoid unnecessary type assertions.
Prefer immutable data patterns where practical.
Use meaningful names.
Avoid overly clever TypeScript.
Templates
Keep templates readable.
Avoid deeply nested structures.
Avoid duplicated template logic.
Prefer Angular control flow syntax.
Use accessible semantic HTML.
Avoid unnecessary DOM elements.
RxJS
Use RxJS when dealing with asynchronous streams or external reactive APIs.
Do not introduce RxJS solely for simple local state.
Avoid unnecessarily complex observable chains.
Accessibility
Use semantic HTML.
Provide accessible labels for interactive elements.
Ensure keyboard navigation works.
Do not rely exclusively on color to communicate information.
Preserve visible focus states.